+# The Daily Grind
+
+The homepage is static and needs no build. Seasonal Favorites are HTML strings in
+`seasonal-favorites.mjs`, inserted through `safe-html.mjs`. Native `setHTML()` is
+preferred; other browsers load the local DOMPurify fallback with the same narrow
+tag/attribute allowlist. A CSP meta tag enforces Trusted Types for DOM sinks where
+supported, allowing only DOMPurify's policy. Browsers without Trusted Types still
+sanitize all card HTML. Sanitizer failures display a plain-text message.
+
+Run `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` and `pnpm test` for automated DOM/security
+checks. These tests use jsdom; they do not validate native browser CSP enforcement
+or the native Sanitizer implementation.
+
+`vendor/` contains DOMPurify 3.4.17 and its license so deployment requires no CDN
+or access to `node_modules`. After upgrading the pinned dependency, run
+`pnpm run vendor:dompurify`, run the tests, and commit the refreshed vendor files
+and lockfile together.
